<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35592" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔνθηρος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θήρ</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>full of wild beasts, haunted, infested by them,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					289
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ichn.</u>
					216
				</span></i>
			; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὗλαι</span>] [<i><span class="en">
				Arr.
			</span></i>]<i><span class="en">
				<u>Peripl.M.Eux.</u>
				12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>wild, rough,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιθέντες ἔ. τρίχα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					562
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. πούς</span>
			<i>'angry',</i> of the ulcerated foot of Philoctetes, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				698
			</span></i> (not 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θηρόδηκτος</span>
			, as Sch.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἔ.</span>”
				<i>savagery,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					6.63
				</span></i>
			.</div>
